body:
Phase 3 step 2 of `docs/design/engine-code-to-omni.md`, for PostgreSQL: metadata-to-metadata migrations are generated by omni's catalog (`LoadMetadata` with `Full`, then `Diff` and `GenerateMigration`, minus the `bbdataarchive` schema) instead of Bytebase's differ and `pg/metadata_migration.go`. This is the PostgreSQL counterpart of #22037 (MySQL), and independent of it.

## What routes where

The metadata diff (`schema.DiffMigration`) serves the Schema Editor (`DatabaseService.DiffMetadata`), Sync Schema against a changelog, and changelog rollback. SDL rollouts already ran on omni and are unchanged.

| Engine | Before | After |
| --- | --- | --- |
| PostgreSQL | Bytebase differ + `pg/metadata_migration.go` | omni `pg/catalog` (`catalog_migration.go`) |
| CockroachDB | Bytebase differ + `pg/metadata_migration.go` | unchanged |

`omniDiffMetadataMigration` loads each snapshot under its database's configured search path, as walk-through does. An object omni cannot install as the snapshot defines it (a stand-in or a missing object) is harmless when it is identical on both sides, because both loads agree on it. When it differs, the diff refuses with an error naming the object rather than comparing stand-ins. Table statistics (row count, sizes) are not part of that comparison.

## What stays, and why

CockroachDB keeps every piece of the old path:
- `pg/metadata_migration.go`;
- the writer copies in `pg/get_database_definition.go` it renders with;
- `differ.go` and the comparers, which TiDB, MSSQL, Oracle, MariaDB and OceanBase also use.

`metadata_migration_test.go`'s 70 hand-written cases now run as CockroachDB (renamed `TestCockroachMetadataDiff*`), since that is the code they cover. One case duplicated an existing CockroachDB test and is dropped. `FilterPostgresArchiveSchema` was called only by its test and is deleted.

## Fixtures and omni changes

PostgreSQL had no migration golden; its cases are hand-written assertions. The differential run below replayed them (86 PostgreSQL inputs) plus 32 pairs of successive `LATEST.sql` revisions through both generators, applying each migration to PostgreSQL 17 and comparing the synced result with the target. Where omni fell short, it was fixed in omni first, each fix with an oracle test against PostgreSQL 17.12:
- bytebase/omni#1058: type drops wait until the migration stops using the type.
- bytebase/omni#1062:
  - partition children install as `PARTITION OF`, and subpartitions get their own `PARTITION BY`;
  - non-serial owned sequences are created and owned;
  - extensions are created, dropped and updated, and their own objects are left out;
  - composite and column `COLLATE` are written, and comments are loaded;
  - expression index keys are parenthesised, keeping operator classes;
  - constraint and index columns are compared by name rather than attnum, so a column inserted mid-table no longer rebuilds the key and every FK on it;
  - FK drops run first;
  - sequences are released or dropped in the righ

